  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage increase occurs when the campus population doubles in one month? The number of students on campus triples at the end of every month. There are 12 students on campus at the beginning of the year. Percentage increase is calculated relative to the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Initial population: \\(12\\) students.\n\nAfter one month, the population triples:\n\n\\[\n12 \\times 3 = 36\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n36-12=24\n\\]\n\nRelative to the original population, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{24}{12}\\times 100\\% = 200\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{200\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Solve this problem step by step. Put you\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. The number of students on campus doubles at the end of every month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Initial population:\n\n\\[\n12 \\text{ students}\n\\]\n\nAfter doubling in one month:\n\n\\[\n12 \\times 2 = 24 \\text{ students}\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n24-12=12 \\text{ students}\n\\]\n\nPercentage increase relative to the original population:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{12}{12}\\times 100\\% = 100\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. There are 10 students on campus at the beginning of the year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The initial campus population is \\(10\\) students.\n\nAfter doubling in one month:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2 = 20\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n20-10=10\n\\]\n\nThus, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\% = 100\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: the student population is multiplied by 2 after each completed month.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Starting with \\(10\\) students, after one completed month the population is multiplied by \\(2\\):\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2 = 20\n\\]\n\nThe increase is:\n\n\\[\n20-10=10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the percentage increase is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{10}\\times 100\\% = 100\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{100\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many students will be on campus after three completed months?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Starting with \\(10\\) students and multiplying by \\(2\\) after each completed month:\n\n- After 1 month: \\(10 \\times 2 = 20\\)\n- After 2 months: \\(20 \\times 2 = 40\\)\n- After 3 months: \\(40 \\times 2 = 80\\)\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: A doubling means the new population is twice the original population.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Yes. Since each doubling makes the population twice its size at the start of that month:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^3 = 10 \\times 8 = 80\n\\]\n\nAfter three completed months, there will be:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80\\text{ students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many additional students would have joined campus by the end of May beyond the students present at the beginning of the year? One more thing you should know: the question concerns the number of students on campus by the end of May.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "There are \\(5\\) completed months from the beginning of the year through the end of May. The population doubles each month:\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 2^5 = 10 \\times 32 = 320\n\\]\n\nSo, by the end of May, there are \\(320\\) students on campus.\n\nThe number of additional students beyond the \\(10\\) present at the beginning of the year is:\n\n\\[\n320-10=310\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{310\\text{ additional students}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
